<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===================================================================================
  revised-ontology.owl  (Day 3 Exercise, Step 5)
  University Courses domain — BFO 2020 / CCO / IAO aligned.
  Author: Ryan Riccucci

  This file corrects generated-ontology.owl. The evaluation is embedded below so the
  submission travels as the three required files with no separate write-up.

  For portability this file DECLARES the handful of BFO/RO/IAO terms it reuses as
  local stub classes/properties (with their canonical OBO IRIs and labels) instead of
  owl:import-ing the full BFO 2020 + CCO. In production, replace the "Imported upper-
  ontology stubs" block with:
      <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo.owl"/>
      <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://.../MergedAllCoreOntology.ttl"/>  (CCO)
  The stubs are logically inert (no extra axioms), so a reasoner result on this file
  is preserved after swapping in the real imports.

  ===================================================================================
  EVALUATION — at least five substantive issues in generated-ontology.owl
  ===================================================================================

  Framework note: "Logical consistency is necessary, but not sufficient for
  ontological adequacy." The generated file is FIRST inconsistent (Issue 5); but even
  after the single offending axiom is removed it remains ontologically WRONG
  (Issues 1–4, 6). The reasoner only catches Issue 5. That gap is the whole lesson.

  =================================================================================
  ISSUE 1 — ONTOLOGICAL / CATEGORICAL ERROR: roles modeled as rigid kinds.
    Generated: Student ⊑ Person and Professor ⊑ Person, asserted owl:disjointWith.
    Diagnosis: "student" and "instructor" are ROLES (BFO:0000023, realizable
      entities) that a person BEARS contingently and can drop — not species of the
      material entity Person. Being a student is not what a person IS; it is a role
      inhering in her. Modeling them as disjoint rigid kinds also makes the true
      statement "a grad TA is both" contradictory (see Issue 5).
    Fix: introduce StudentRole and InstructorRole ⊑ BFO:Role; a Person bears them via
      hasRole (RO:0000053 'bearer of'). Roles are NOT disjoint; one person bears both.

  =================================================================================
  ISSUE 2 — ONTOLOGICAL / CATEGORICAL ERROR: information conflated with its referent
             (and continuant conflated with occurrent).
    Generated: a single class Course carries the catalog title AND is the thing a
      professor "teaches" AND the thing a student is "enrolledIn". One class is doing
      the work of three different kinds of entity.
    Diagnosis: the catalog "course" is an INFORMATION CONTENT ENTITY / plan
      specification (a generically dependent continuant, BFO:0000031). What a
      professor actually does, and what a student participates in, is the OFFERING —
      an occurrent (process). Catalog-CS101 is not taught; the Fall-2025 offering of
      CS101 is.
    Fix: split Course (GDC / ICE, the catalog entity) from CourseOffering
      (BFO:Process, the scheduled delivery). Course is offeredAs CourseOffering;
      teaching and enrollment attach to the offering, not the catalog entity.

  =================================================================================
  ISSUE 3 — PROCESS MISREPRESENTED AS A CONTINUANT.
    Generated: Enrollment is a bare class with a data property enrollmentDate — a
      static thing that "has a date". The rdfs:comment ("When a student enrolls…")
      even admits it is an event.
    Diagnosis: enrollment is an OCCURRENT (BFO:Process). A process unfolds in time and
      HAS PARTICIPANTS; it does not "have a date" as an attribute — it occupies a
      temporal region.
    Fix: EnrollmentProcess ⊑ BFO:Process; hasParticipant some Person (bearing a
      StudentRole); occupiesTemporalRegion some temporal region.

  =================================================================================
  ISSUE 4 — DEFINITION PROBLEMS: circular and metalinguistic definitions.
    Generated:
      • Course: "A Course is a course that is offered by a university." — CIRCULAR;
        the genus repeats the definiendum ("a course is a course").
      • Student: "A class that represents students." — METALINGUISTIC; defines the
        OWL class artifact, not the entity, and is also circular ("students").
    Diagnosis: violates genus–differentia form (an X is a [broader kind] that
      [differentia]). A definition may not contain the term being defined, and must
      define the entity, not the representation.
    Fix: real definitions, e.g. Course = "a directive information content entity that
      prescribes the content, credit value, and prerequisites of a unit of
      instruction offered by a department."

  =================================================================================
  ISSUE 5 — LOGICAL / OWL MODELING ISSUE (reasoner-detectable INCONSISTENCY),
             plus a latent over-restriction.
    Generated: individual JaneDoe is asserted rdf:type Student AND Professor, which are
      owl:disjointWith → the ontology is INCONSISTENT (HermiT/ELK: unsatisfiable).
      Separately, hasInstructor is declared owl:FunctionalProperty, hard-capping every
      course at ≤1 instructor and silently forbidding co-teaching / multiple sections
      — a modeling error the reasoner will NOT flag until two distinct instructors are
      asserted.
    Diagnosis: the inconsistency is a symptom of Issue 1 (wrong kinds), not an
      independent bug — deleting the disjointness axiom would make the file consistent
      yet still ontologically wrong. The functional property encodes a false universal.
    Fix: remove the Student/Professor disjointness (roles handle it, Issue 1); drop
      FunctionalProperty. If a cardinality claim is wanted, put a justified one on the
      OFFERING (e.g., an offering has ≥1 instructor-role participant), not a functional
      global.

  =================================================================================
  ISSUE 6 — RELATIONS PROBLEMS.
    Generated:
      (a) hasPrerequisite is NOT declared transitive, yet prerequisite chains are
          transitive: CS301→CS201→CS101 should entail CS301→CS101. As written, the
          transitive competency question (CQ2) fails.
      (b) belongsTo (Course→Department) is a vague catch-all relation name; and
          Prerequisite is reified as a CLASS ("every noun a class") when the relation
          hasPrerequisite already carries the meaning.
      (c) enrolledIn points Student→Course, but a student enrolls in a specific
          OFFERING, not the catalog entity (consequence of Issue 2).
    Fix: hasPrerequisite ⊑ owl:TransitiveProperty; replace belongsTo with the specific
      offeredByDepartment; delete the redundant Prerequisite class; retype enrolledIn
      as Person→CourseOffering.

  =================================================================================
  Also corrected (minor, from "every noun a class"): CreditHour class removed — credit
  is a data property (creditHours, xsd:decimal) of a Course, not a class of objects.
  Grade retyped from a bare class of letters to GradeAssignment, an information content
  entity that is ABOUT a person's performance in an offering.

  ===================================================================================
  REASONER RESULTS (HermiT via owlready2; Protégé "Start reasoner" reproduces this)
    BEFORE (generated-ontology.owl): INCONSISTENT — Student ⊓ Professor = ∅ but
      JaneDoe ∈ both. Protégé flags the ontology inconsistent / owl:Nothing.
    AFTER  (this file):              CONSISTENT — 0 unsatisfiable classes. With
      property-value inference on, hasPrerequisite transitivity entails
      CS301 hasPrerequisite CS101 (verified: CS301 → {CS101, CS201}); the grad TA
      (jsmith) coherently bears both a StudentRole and an InstructorRole.
  ===================================================================================
-->
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://example.org/university-courses#"
     xml:base="http://example.org/university-courses"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:obo="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/"
     xmlns:ex="http://example.org/university-courses#">

    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses">
        <rdfs:comment>University Courses ontology, revised for BFO 2020 / CCO / IAO conformance. Distinguishes the catalog course (information content entity) from its offering (process), models student/instructor as roles, and models enrollment as a process.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>

    <!-- ================= Imported upper-ontology stubs (replace with owl:imports) ================= -->
    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"><rdfs:label>material entity</rdfs:label></owl:Class>
    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"><rdfs:label>role</rdfs:label></owl:Class>
    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"><rdfs:label>process</rdfs:label></owl:Class>
    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"><rdfs:label>generically dependent continuant</rdfs:label></owl:Class>
    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000008"><rdfs:label>temporal region</rdfs:label></owl:Class>
    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027"><rdfs:label>object aggregate</rdfs:label></owl:Class>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"><rdfs:label>bearer of</rdfs:label></owl:ObjectProperty>
    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000057"><rdfs:label>has participant</rdfs:label></owl:ObjectProperty>
    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000199"><rdfs:label>occupies temporal region</rdfs:label></owl:ObjectProperty>
    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"><rdfs:label>is about</rdfs:label></owl:ObjectProperty>

    <!-- ================= Domain Classes ================= -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#Person">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A material entity that is a human being enrolled in, employed by, or otherwise participating in university activities.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#StudentRole">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A role that is borne by a person in virtue of being admitted to and enrolled in a program or offering, and that is realized in taking courses.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#InstructorRole">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A role that is borne by a person in virtue of being assigned to deliver a course offering, and that is realized in teaching it.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#Course">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A directive information content entity that prescribes the subject matter, credit value, and prerequisites of a unit of instruction offered by a department; the catalog entity, as distinct from any particular offering of it.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#CourseOffering">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A process that is the scheduled delivery of a course during a specific semester, having an instructor and enrolled students as participants.</rdfs:comment>
        <!-- Justified cardinality on the OFFERING (replaces the functional hasInstructor bug): every offering has at least one participant bearing an instructor role. -->
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#Person"/>
                            <owl:Restriction>
                                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
                                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#InstructorRole"/>
                            </owl:Restriction>
                        </owl:intersectionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#EnrollmentProcess">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A process in which a person bearing a student role becomes and remains registered as a participant in a course offering over a temporal interval.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#Department">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027"/>
        <rdfs:comment>An object aggregate that is an organizational unit of a university responsible for offering courses in one or more subject areas.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#Semester">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000008"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A temporal region that is an academic term during which course offerings are delivered.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#GradeAssignment">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
        <rdfs:comment>An information content entity that records the evaluated result a person achieved in a course offering, and that is about that person's performance.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>

    <!-- ================= Object Properties ================= -->

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#hasRole">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Person"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a person to a role that inheres in and is borne by that person.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#offeredAs">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CourseOffering"/>
        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#offeringOf"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a catalog course to a scheduled offering that realizes it.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#offeringOf">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CourseOffering"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a course offering to the catalog course it realizes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#hasPrerequisite">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a course to a course that must be completed before it; transitive, so prerequisite chains are entailed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#offeredByDepartment">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Department"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a course to the department responsible for offering it.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#enrolledIn">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Person"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CourseOffering"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a person bearing a student role to a course offering in which they are registered.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#gradeAbout">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#GradeAssignment"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Person"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Relates a grade assignment to the person whose performance it records.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>

    <!-- ================= Data Properties ================= -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#courseCode">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#courseTitle">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#creditHours">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The credit value of a course. Credit is a data value of a course, not a class of objects (the generated CreditHour class was removed).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#gradeValue">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#GradeAssignment"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>

    <!-- ================= Individuals ================= -->

    <!-- The graduate TA: one person, two roles, now fully consistent. -->
    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#jsmith">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Person"/>
        <hasRole rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#jsmith_studentRole"/>
        <hasRole rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#jsmith_instructorRole"/>
        <enrolledIn rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CS301_Fall2025"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#jsmith_studentRole">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#StudentRole"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#jsmith_instructorRole">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#InstructorRole"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#CS_Department">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Department"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#CS101">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <courseCode>CS101</courseCode>
        <courseTitle>Introduction to Computer Science</courseTitle>
        <creditHours rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">3.0</creditHours>
        <offeredByDepartment rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CS_Department"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#CS201">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <courseCode>CS201</courseCode>
        <hasPrerequisite rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CS101"/>
        <offeredByDepartment rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CS_Department"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

    <!-- Transitivity: CS301→CS201→CS101 entails CS301 hasPrerequisite CS101 (CQ2). -->
    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#CS301">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Course"/>
        <courseCode>CS301</courseCode>
        <hasPrerequisite rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CS201"/>
        <offeredByDepartment rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CS_Department"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#Fall2025">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Semester"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#CS301_Fall2025">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CourseOffering"/>
        <offeringOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#CS301"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000199 rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#Fall2025"/>
        <obo:BFO_0000057 rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#jsmith"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://example.org/university-courses#Grade_jsmith_CS301">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#GradeAssignment"/>
        <gradeAbout rdf:resource="http://example.org/university-courses#jsmith"/>
        <gradeValue>A</gradeValue>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>

</rdf:RDF>
